## Service Architecture

[3–5 sentences describing the service design. Example for Express:]

```
Express HTTP service handling order processing for the billing domain.
Reads user profiles from auth-service; writes payout events via Kafka producer.
All database access via Prisma with explicit $transaction blocks for multi-row writes.
Financial endpoints require idempotency-key header; idempotency rows enforce uniqueness at DB level.
```

[Or for NestJS:]

```
NestJS service organized by feature module (orders, payments, payouts).
Each module: controller (HTTP) + service (business logic) + repository (DB) + DTO (validation).
Global ValidationPipe + class-validator on all DTOs. Global ExceptionFilter normalizes errors.
TypeORM with explicit transaction managers for financial mutations.
```

