## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first (Express layout):
- `src/app.ts` or `src/main.ts` — entry point, middleware wiring, route registration
- `src/routes/` — Express routers; thin handlers, delegate to services
- `src/controllers/` — request parsing, response shaping (NestJS only)
- `src/services/` — business logic and orchestration (no DB calls here)
- `src/repositories/` — all database access via [Prisma|TypeORM]
- `src/middleware/` — cross-cutting concerns: auth, logging, rate limiting
- `src/dto/` — request/response shapes; validated at the boundary
- `tests/` — `*.test.ts` or `*.spec.ts` alongside source

Layers and their purpose:
- `routes/` or `controllers/` → Parse request, validate via DTO, route to service (≤50 lines each)
- `services/` → Business logic, orchestration across repositories (no direct DB queries)
- `repositories/` → All database access; single DB concern per file
- `middleware/` → Auth, logging, rate limiting, request context
- `dto/` → Plain data classes; validation decorators (class-validator) or schemas (zod)
- `tests/` → Real-persistence-path tests for P1/P2/P3 (see `node-patterns.md`)

